      "id": "2120439243478806562",
      "text": "RT @Dogetothemoon: Elon Musk has a track record of calling hard problems early.\n\nIn a February 2026 interview, he warned: “Those who have l…",
      "created_at": "Wed Nov 11 08:51:26 +0000 2026",
      "lang": "en",
      "media": [],
      "retweet": {
        "id": "2110140249141821578",
        "text": "Elon Musk has a track record of calling hard problems early.\n\nIn a February 2026 interview, he warned: “Those who have lived in software land don’t realize they’re about to have a hard lesson in hardware.”\n\nBy late August, SpaceX confirmed it was bringing the casting of gas-turbine blades and vanes in-house — the single biggest bottleneck for new natural-gas power plants needed to feed AI data centers. Musk said the move could bring turbines online up to 18 months faster.\n\nToday he put it even more bluntly: SpaceX has “a super cracked team that is outperforming the rest of the world by an order of magnitude in mass to orbit — and even we find it very difficult.”\n\nHardware doesn’t care about demos, funding rounds, or slide decks. The teams that actually build the hard stuff keep winning.\n\nWhat a legend.",
        "created_at": "Tue Oct 13 22:46:54 +0000 2026",
        "lang": "en",
        "media": [
          {
            "type": "video",
            "id": "2110136316113649665",
            "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2110136316113649665/vid/avc1/1280x720/6Zx-3vRMop3Qztuu.mp4?tag=29",
            "bitrate": 2176000
          }
        ],
        "retweet": null,
        "quoted": {
          "id": "2110122281603326170",
          "text": "It’s not that supercomputer data centers are not in high demand, as they definitely are. However, getting money to build complex hardware systems with massive power, cooling & networking is not the same as doing it. \n\nSpaceX has a super cracked team that is outperforming the rest of the world by an order of magnitude in mass to orbit and even we find it very difficult!",
          "created_at": "Tue Oct 13 21:35:30 +0000 2026",
          "lang": "en",
          "media": [],
          "retweet": null,
          "quoted": null,
          "user": {
            "id": "44196397",
